---
title: Privacy
description: >-
  What Level Up Civics collects, why, and how it is handled.
---
{% extends "layouts/base.njk" %}

{% block head %}
<style>
  .privacy-body { max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .privacy-body h2 {
    font-family: 'Big Shoulders Display', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 700; font-size: 24px; color: var(--ink);
    margin: 48px 0 12px;
  }
  .privacy-body h2:first-of-type { margin-top: 0; }
  .privacy-body p,
  .privacy-body li {
    font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--gray);
  }
  .privacy-body ul { padding-left: 20px; margin: 12px 0; }
  .privacy-body li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .privacy-updated {
    font-size: 13px; color: var(--gray); margin-top: 48px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--soft); padding-top: 24px;
  }
</style>
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}

<div class="page-hero" style="min-height: auto;">
  <div class="page-hero-content">
    <div class="page-hero-eyebrow">Privacy</div>
    <h1 class="page-hero-h1">Privacy Statement</h1>
    <p class="page-hero-sub">
      Level Up Civics Foundation takes privacy seriously. This page explains what we collect, why, and how it is handled.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<section class="sec sec-cream">
  <div class="privacy-body">

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>When an educator registers a team or submits a project entry through our Google Form, we collect:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Advisor name, school email, school name, and county</li>
      <li>Team member first and last names and grade levels</li>
      <li>Project information (title, community challenge, summary)</li>
      <li>Video walkthrough files or links submitted as part of the entry</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
    <p>We use this information to administer the Battle of the Counties competition: to identify participating schools and teams, to route entries to judges, and to coordinate county finals and the statewide championship.</p>

    <h2>Who sees it</h2>
    <p>Submitted information is accessible to Level Up Civics Foundation staff, competition judges, and the county offices of education coordinating your county's program. We do not sell, rent, or share personal information with third parties for marketing purposes.</p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>Registration and submission data is retained through the end of the competition year (the current program year concludes after the January 2027 Statewide Championship). After the program year, identifying student information is deleted. Aggregate and anonymized program data may be retained for reporting purposes.</p>

    <h2>Student privacy and media releases</h2>
    <p>Level Up Civics does not collect information directly from students. All team information is submitted by the school's advisor. Parent/guardian permissions and media releases stay on file with the school, district, or county office of education. The submitting advisor attests that the required permissions are complete before entering a team.</p>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <p>Our registration form is hosted on Google Forms. Submitted data is stored in Google Workspace. Video files may be hosted on YouTube, Google Drive, or another platform chosen by the submitting school. Each of these services has its own privacy policy.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>For questions about this privacy statement or how your information is handled, contact us at <a href="mailto:info@levelupcivicsfoundation.org">info@levelupcivicsfoundation.org</a>.</p>

    <p class="privacy-updated">Last updated: September 2026</p>
  </div>
</section>

{% endblock %}
